1
00:00:22,510 --> 00:00:23,890
Your eye is next.

2
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:25,840
Show me you're afraid.

3
00:00:27,810 --> 00:00:28,890
Don't, Fox!

4
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:37,590
Snake...

5
00:00:41,350 --> 00:00:45,086
Aw, man. He's in rough shape.

6
00:00:45,110 --> 00:00:50,040
B-Boss, welcome back.
Wh-Wh-When did you get here?

7
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:52,290
Fox.

8
00:00:52,790 --> 00:00:53,920
Yes, sir.

9
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:56,486
Come closer.

10
00:00:56,510 --> 00:00:57,650
Y-Yes, sir.

11
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:08,626
Badger.

12
00:01:08,650 --> 00:01:09,840
Yes, sir!

13
00:01:10,310 --> 00:01:11,570
Explain.

14
00:01:14,630 --> 00:01:16,660
Yes, sir.

15
00:01:20,390 --> 00:01:21,650
Idiots.

16
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:27,740
You're a bunch of idiots.

17
00:01:27,990 --> 00:01:28,446
Awakening.

18
00:01:28,470 --> 00:01:32,006
What's the point of
you guys bullying the slaves?

19
00:01:32,030 --> 00:01:34,210
The young master's gotta do it himself.

20
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:36,816
Yeah, b-but he...

21
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:42,100
H-He... got cheeky with us, so...

22
00:01:59,540 --> 00:02:03,480
Sorry. These guys are idiots.

23
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:07,220
I'm Snake.

24
00:02:09,270 --> 00:02:10,390
I'm Thorfinn.

25
00:02:57,940 --> 00:02:59,830
See that, Thorfinn?

26
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:04,600
Your body says it wants to live.

27
00:03:13,420 --> 00:03:14,626
I'm going to sleep.

28
00:03:14,650 --> 00:03:17,940
You guys had better
graciously see them back home.

29
00:03:21,030 --> 00:03:22,960
I know I don't have to tell you...

30
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:28,420
that the day you cause
any more trouble over this matter,

31
00:03:29,330 --> 00:03:35,190
you won't be able to chew
your own food anymore.

32
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:39,396
I didn't hear a "Yes, sir."

33
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:40,880
Yes, sir!

34
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:49,600
Thorfinn, you...

35
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:55,140
Do I want to live?

36
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:02,400
Live...

37
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:10,420
Live, and do what?

38
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:01,650
I see.

39
00:06:02,450 --> 00:06:06,240
Besides your ear,
none of your injuries are very deep.

40
00:06:07,430 --> 00:06:09,480
Once they're healed, you'll be good as new.

41
00:06:13,230 --> 00:06:16,756
I'm sorry you two had to go through that.

42
00:06:16,780 --> 00:06:22,530
The master doesn't know what to do
about his guests' misbehavior either.

43
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:24,420
"Misbehavior?"

44
00:06:24,870 --> 00:06:27,520
Their "misbehavior" nearly got us killed.

45
00:06:28,250 --> 00:06:32,160
It's not as though
they'd actually kill you.

46
00:06:33,590 --> 00:06:34,480
You're wrong.

47
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:40,340
If their boss Snake hadn't shown up,
they really would've killed us.

48
00:06:42,180 --> 00:06:48,470
Guys like them think our lives are
worth less than those of insects.

49
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:52,900
Either way, we couldn't help it.

50
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:58,400
The strong kill the weak.

51
00:06:59,570 --> 00:07:01,120
It's only natural.

52
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:06,096
What did you just say?

53
00:07:06,120 --> 00:07:08,200
Now, now, Einar.

54
00:07:09,030 --> 00:07:14,520
If they try to mess with you again,
come talk to me instead of going with them.

55
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:18,846
More importantly,
we can't allow your wounds to fester.

56
00:07:18,870 --> 00:07:20,380
I'll put some medicine on them.

57
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:22,640
Medicine?

58
00:07:22,990 --> 00:07:25,906
U-Uh, Pater, we don't...

59
00:07:25,930 --> 00:07:28,760
Don't worry about paying
me for the medicine.

60
00:07:29,230 --> 00:07:33,090
It's my responsibility
to look after you two.

61
00:07:34,580 --> 00:07:38,020
I'm sorry I struck a nerve.

62
00:07:40,740 --> 00:07:44,790
No, it's fine. Thank you.

63
00:07:46,590 --> 00:07:50,500
You'd better thank Arnheid, too.

64
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:56,020
She ran all around the farm
to tell me what happened.

65
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:05,856
Rest for today.

66
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:09,006
I'll talk to the master about it.

67
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:10,270
Also...

68
00:08:10,790 --> 00:08:13,846
It's one of my old shirts,
so it's probably a bit large for you,

69
00:08:13,870 --> 00:08:15,770
but Thorfinn, you can have this.

70
00:08:16,140 --> 00:08:20,020
After all, yours is full of holes
after what they did.

71
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:31,410
Don't you have anything to say to Pater?

72
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:42,496
Listen, you. You're supposed to say
"thank you" in these situations.

73
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:43,270
Go on.

74
00:08:48,910 --> 00:08:50,360
Say it.

75
00:08:51,660 --> 00:08:54,366
Why haven't you been
saying anything, anyway?

76
00:08:54,390 --> 00:08:57,670
It's not nice,
when everyone's being kind to you.

77
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:03,160
It's fine. I know Thorfinn
doesn't say much.

78
00:09:10,130 --> 00:09:11,490
Thank you.

79
00:09:31,630 --> 00:09:33,800
Hey, where are you going?

80
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:38,210
He said we don't have to
harvest wheat today.

81
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:40,810
I'm going to the woods.

82
00:09:41,350 --> 00:09:43,190
These injuries are nothing.

83
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:53,160
Wait up. I'll go with you.

84
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:31,440
The way he moved when Snake attacked him...

85
00:10:34,130 --> 00:10:35,800
He's no ordinary man.

86
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:39,720
And...

87
00:10:43,990 --> 00:10:46,850
The strong kill the weak.

88
00:10:48,710 --> 00:10:50,680
It's only natural.

89
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:00,150
Thorfinn.

90
00:11:04,770 --> 00:11:08,530
Have you ever been to war?

91
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:13,840
Yes.

92
00:11:20,770 --> 00:11:24,120
Have you killed people?

93
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:27,200
Yes.

94
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:37,620
How many?

95
00:11:39,780 --> 00:11:43,250
Five men? Ten?

96
00:11:49,670 --> 00:11:51,640
Why do you want to know?

97
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:55,520
I thought you didn't like war.

98
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:00,210
Timber.

99
00:12:22,660 --> 00:12:24,980
I don't remember how many.

100
00:12:28,610 --> 00:12:30,320
I've killed a lot of people.

101
00:12:32,850 --> 00:12:36,950
I was on the battlefield since
around the time I was five or six.

102
00:12:38,230 --> 00:12:41,440
I joined the Danish army's
invasion of England.

103
00:12:49,110 --> 00:12:51,600
I was a warrior.

104
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:58,040
Do you hate me now, Einar?

105
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:50,260
I was a warrior.

106
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:54,230
Do you hate me now, Einar?

107
00:14:37,620 --> 00:14:40,200
I don't remember how many.

108
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:55,880
I've killed a lot of people.

109
00:16:15,370 --> 00:16:17,880
Found you.

110
00:16:20,710 --> 00:16:27,510
Damn kid. Die!

111
00:16:36,450 --> 00:16:38,790
You brat.

112
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:45,450
Kill. Kill him. Die!

113
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:14,640
Damn it!

114
00:18:47,810 --> 00:18:48,790
Einar...

115
00:18:53,890 --> 00:18:59,590
Why do you wake me
every time I cry out in my sleep?

116
00:19:12,770 --> 00:19:17,280
I've killed people. I've
killed a lot of people.

117
00:19:19,110 --> 00:19:26,080
From battle to battle, I've attacked
villages and killed a lot of people.

118
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:33,400
I'm no different from the people

119
00:19:36,080 --> 00:19:37,680
who killed your family.

120
00:19:57,070 --> 00:19:58,320
Do you...

121
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:04,040
Does anything good come from being alive?

122
00:20:07,510 --> 00:20:08,920
Not for me.

123
00:20:12,760 --> 00:20:20,100
Not a single good thing has
happened to me in my entire life.

124
00:20:30,310 --> 00:20:34,240
Do you want to die?

125
00:20:35,340 --> 00:20:40,196
I don't know what kind of
terrible fate you've suffered.

126
00:20:40,220 --> 00:20:43,750
I don't want to know what kind of hell
you've lived through, either.

127
00:20:45,170 --> 00:20:53,950
But we're able to chit-chat,
eat, shit, and sleep in this hell...

128
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:06,420
because someone kept us alive.

129
00:21:08,550 --> 00:21:10,340
How can you say nothing good's
ever happened to you?

130
00:21:17,170 --> 00:21:18,440
You're wrong.

131
00:21:21,510 --> 00:21:23,280
You're wrong!

132
00:21:26,850 --> 00:21:27,920
Asshole.

133
00:21:30,290 --> 00:21:31,800
Don't act so spoiled.

134
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:00,040
Besides...

135
00:22:02,270 --> 00:22:06,660
It's not like you killed my family.

136
00:22:10,920 --> 00:22:12,530
Don't be so arrogant.

137
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:30,400
Thank you, Einar.

138
00:22:33,410 --> 00:22:37,550
Thank you for waking me.

139
00:22:45,310 --> 00:22:46,390
Jeez...

140
00:22:47,370 --> 00:22:51,380
I can't get enough sleep because
you won't stop talking in yours.

141
00:22:54,050 --> 00:22:55,240
I see.

142
00:23:01,240 --> 00:23:03,316
I'm sorry, Einar.

143
00:23:03,340 --> 00:23:05,110
Just go to sleep already.

144
00:25:36,350 --> 00:25:37,776
Path of Blood.

145
00:25:37,800 --> 00:25:39,300
"Path of Blood."
